From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:05:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: the Social Club layout holds only its anchors; the
 rest at the first ask

PLA-842 (decision 0183, amending 0169). The layout held about 30 GiB of
the guest window from boot. It now holds from boot only the anchors the
helper's 64 GiB window forces, each sized from the PLA-841 census:

- libcef's pool prefix at 0x7000000000, held from exec by the host's low
  hold (iOS otherwise takes that address during exec): 64 MiB, was 256;
- chrome_elf's pool prefix at 0x7800000000: 64 MiB, was 4 GiB;
- Oilpan, 16 GiB above chrome_elf's base, at 0x7c00000000: 512 MiB, was
  1 GiB; FEX's arena now starts at its end, 0x7c20000000;
- ELF_META at 0x7400000000, the upper half of libcef's pool, where
  libcef's PartitionAlloc commits: 1 GiB, was 6.25 GiB. H1 was not
  settled by the census (every attributed commit there is libcef's, at
  stack word 4, never 0), so it stays an anchor, the conservative
  reading; it becomes on demand only if a census shows no libcef commit
  there and chrome_elf's at word 0.

An anchor's size is the highest committed end any phone run measured in
it, rounded up to a power of two, times four, at least 64 MiB:
libcef's and chrome_elf's 0x5000 and Oilpan's 0x6420000
(pla841-rdr2-census5), ELF_META's 0xaa82000 (l5).

libcef's metadata (1 GiB), V8's cage (8 GiB, 4 GiB-aligned) and V8's
code range (1 GiB, 4 GiB-aligned; a new kind 7) are on demand: nothing is
held until the helper's first ask places one, at its home when that is
free (0x78c0000000, 0x7a00000000, 0x7700000000), else at the highest
free base aligned as it needs, from the window's free runs as the
elastic policy reads them. From then on it is held in place like an
anchor (0231), so the next helper gets the same range; one whose range
something else mapped is placed anew at the next ask. The code range's
hinted retry over [0x7100000000, 0x7400000000) (0243) goes: the router
serves that ask first.

ELF_META2 (0228) and RDR2's 8,960 MiB game hold go: the game's pools are
the elastic policy's, as in any Play. The JIT pool's RW alias stays where
the host maps it at exec, 0x7900000000, and must end below Oilpan's
anchor. The census's kinds follow: the slots, V8's code range among them,
and the JIT pool's RW alias.

Linear: PLA-842
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-13-sc-census-rdr2.md; tools/tests/test_sc_layout.py, test_sc_vm.py, test_sc_boot.py, test_sc_census.py, test_elastic_reserve.py (host checks; phone gates not run)
Offered-upstream: no
